# KNOWN idiom debt, one TAB-separated site per line: a rule's kind, its
# file, and its own source line trimmed. This file only ever SHRINKS —
# `avra check --baseline_accept` prunes what a fix made gone, and no
# path through it ADDS a line: a new site is fixed in the code, or a
# human adds the line here, reviewed at adoption and every time after
# (CLAUDE.md's baseline law). `avra check --baseline <this file>` gates.
